  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let cd(G) be the set of all complex irreducible character degrees of a finite\ngroup G. Huppert’s Conjecture: if H is a nonabelian simple group and G is any finite\ngroup such that cd(G) = cd(H), then G ∼ = H × A, where A is an abelian group.\n                                                                          H. P. Tong-Viet",
